     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Prequel 1: sometimes it might be useful to try non-default sampler parameters (see: <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/Fl3RBPscUXo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/stan-users/Fl3RBPscUXo&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467613258000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1rfsyLoYxhR-e5V6yEmnNT\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/Fl3RBPscUXo</a>)<br>Prequel 2: one could merge chains coming from different algorithms and/or iter/warmup/thin settings (as long as n_save and warmup2 are equal) and/or &quot;controls&quot;, as they are named now (see: <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/sCLQYj02tB8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/stan-users/sCLQYj02tB8&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467613258000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0AXRv__CvjvH35mb7-Ik-z\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/sCLQYj02tB8</a>)<br><br>So I&#39;m writing/rewriting some rstan functions. A few examples follow.<br><br>Let sm be a compiled stan model.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> warmup </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">250</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thin </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> algorithm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;HMC&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;NUTS&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;NUTS&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> control </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">adapt_delta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.61</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> int_time </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                      metric </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;unit_e&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stepsize </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                 list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">adapt_delta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.62</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max_treedepth </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                      metric </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;unit_e&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stepsize </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                 list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">adapt_delta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.63</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max_treedepth </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                      metric </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;diag_e&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stepsize </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sflist </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mclapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectCores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampling</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chain_id </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> seed </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12345</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                        iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> warmup </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> warmup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thin </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                        algorithm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> algorithm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> control </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> control</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sf </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sflist2stanfit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sflist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>I&#39;d love to add a fourth case, but setting metric = dense_e doesn&#39;t work now (<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/AJXmiruMiSA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/stan-users/AJXmiruMiSA&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467613258000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0EVtQSMoqRdCr4i7thOGaa\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/AJXmiruMiSA</a>).<br><br>I&#39;d like to look at something like:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> get_sampler_config</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>chain_id                </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>algorithm             HMC   NUTS   NUTS<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> int_time           </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.42</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     NA     NA<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max_treedepth        NA     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> metric               NA unit_e diag_e<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stepsize             NA   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.70</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.50</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stepsize_jitter      NA   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>iter                   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>warmup                  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">250</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>thin                    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Adaptation</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> engaged            TRUE   TRUE   TRUE<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gamma              </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> delta              </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.61</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.62</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.63</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa              </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t0                </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>I can now notice that metric and stepsize are not changed when algorithm is &quot;HMC&quot;, but it&#39;ll be soon fixed.<br>Otherwise:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampler_config </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> get_sampler_config</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampler_config<br>  chain_id sampler int_time max_treedepth metric stepsize stepsize_jitter iter<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     HMC </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.424778</span><span style=\"color:#000\">            NA   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       NA              NA   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    NUTS       NA            </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> unit_e      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7</span><span style=\"color:#000\">               </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    NUTS       NA            </span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> diag_e      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#000\">               </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  warmup thin engaged gamma delta kappa t0<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    TRUE  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.61</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    TRUE  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.62</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">250</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    TRUE  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.63</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>A data frame. As to get_sampler_params():<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> get_sampler_params</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Chain</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">HMC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">):</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>              </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1st</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Qu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Median</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mean</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3rd</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Qu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>accept_stat </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2173</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7094</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5975</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>stepsize    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3383</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.5630</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.5630</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.7300</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.671</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4.800</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>int_time    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.4250</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.4250</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.4250</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.4250</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.425</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.425</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Chain</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NUTS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">):</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                 </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1st</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Qu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Median</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mean</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3rd</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Qu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>accept_stat </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.232e-32</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2365</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4477</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5134</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.927</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>stepsize    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4.814e-01</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.5500</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.5500</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.6700</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.572</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.8</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>treedepth   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000e+00</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Chain</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NUTS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">):</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>              </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1st</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Qu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Median</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mean</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3rd</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Qu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>accept_stat  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.02386</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2003</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3332</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5172</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>stepsize     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.896</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.02900</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.1150</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.7140</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.1150</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">11.78</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>treedepth   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Or:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampler_params </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> get_sampler_params</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampler_params<br>   chain algorithm   accept_stat int_time treedepth<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       HMC  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000000e+00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.424778</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        NA<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       HMC  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.805636e-42</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.424778</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        NA<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">29</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      NUTS  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5.472281e-01</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       NA         </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">30</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      NUTS  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.905030e-02</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       NA         </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Another data frame. Furthermore, <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inference</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Stan</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> warmup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>is wrong, because n_save and warmup2 are equal, but iter/warmup/thin are not.<br><br>If someone thinks that such pedantic &quot;improvements&quot; could be useful, I&#39;ll polish up and submit my code.<br><br>Sergio<br><br></div>"
