  {
   "id": "WTsTAOzjx30J",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2013-10-21T21:30:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] RStan: may I submit some code?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "If the RStan developers are interested, the thing to do with it is to\r<br>make a pull request through GitHub.\r<br>\r<br>Then we (and by that I mean Jiqiang or Ben or someone else who\r<br>knows R better than me) can review the code and decide whether to\r<br>merge or to require fixes or other further work.\r<br>\r<br>We want tests and documentation along with pull requests whenever\r<br>possible.  Nothing should get merged into the main development branch\r<br>until that&#39;s done.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On 10/21/13 5:00 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sp_r...@yahoo.it</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; Prequel 1: sometimes it might be useful to try non-default sampler parameters (see:\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/Fl3RBPscUXo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/stan-users/Fl3RBPscUXo&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467613266000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-EB99SULIr8Fg3nRB2tv5\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/Fl3RBPscUXo</a>)\r<br>&gt; Prequel 2: one could merge chains coming from different algorithms and/or iter/warmup/thin settings (as long as n_save\r<br>&gt; and warmup2 are equal) and/or &quot;controls&quot;, as they are named now (see:\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/sCLQYj02tB8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/stan-users/sCLQYj02tB8&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467613266000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0IpNdOQ_M9UTDa4Suk606c\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/sCLQYj02tB8</a>)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; So I&#39;m writing/rewriting some rstan functions. A few examples follow.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Let sm be a compiled stan model.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; iter &lt;- c(10, 100, 500)\r<br>&gt;  &gt; warmup &lt;- c(5, 50, 250)\r<br>&gt;  &gt; thin &lt;- c(1, 10, 50)\r<br>&gt;  &gt; algorithm &lt;- c(&quot;HMC&quot;, &quot;NUTS&quot;, &quot;NUTS&quot;)\r<br>&gt;  &gt; control &lt;- list(list(adapt_delta = 0.61, int_time = 3 * pi,\r<br>&gt; +                      metric = &quot;unit_e&quot;, stepsize = 0.6),\r<br>&gt; +                 list(adapt_delta = 0.62, max_treedepth = 12,\r<br>&gt; +                      metric = &quot;unit_e&quot;, stepsize = 0.7),\r<br>&gt; +                 list(adapt_delta = 0.63, max_treedepth = 15,\r<br>&gt; +                      metric = &quot;diag_e&quot;, stepsize = 0.5))\r<br>&gt;  &gt; sflist &lt;- mclapply(1:3, mc.cores = detectCores(),\r<br>&gt; +                    function(i) sampling(sm, chains = 1, chain_id = i, seed = 12345,\r<br>&gt; +                        iter = iter[i], warmup = warmup[i], thin = thin[i],\r<br>&gt; +                        algorithm = algorithm[i], control = control[[i]]))\r<br>&gt;  &gt; sf &lt;- sflist2stanfit(sflist)\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I&#39;d love to add a fourth case, but setting metric = dense_e doesn&#39;t work now\r<br>&gt; (<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/AJXmiruMiSA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/stan-users/AJXmiruMiSA&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467613266000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0RNSYGVOuVM6POk40skttZ\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/AJXmiruMiSA</a>).\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I&#39;d like to look at something like:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; get_sampler_config(sf)\r<br>&gt; chain_id                1      2      3\r<br>&gt; algorithm             HMC   NUTS   NUTS\r<br>&gt; - int_time           9.42     NA     NA\r<br>&gt; - max_treedepth        NA     12     15\r<br>&gt; - metric               NA unit_e diag_e\r<br>&gt; - stepsize             NA   0.70   0.50\r<br>&gt; - stepsize_jitter      NA   0.00   0.00\r<br>&gt; iter                   10    100    500\r<br>&gt; warmup                  5     50    250\r<br>&gt; thin                    1     10     50\r<br>&gt; Adaptation:\r<br>&gt; - engaged            TRUE   TRUE   TRUE\r<br>&gt; - gamma              0.05   0.05   0.05\r<br>&gt; - delta              0.61   0.62   0.63\r<br>&gt; - kappa              0.75   0.75   0.75\r<br>&gt; - t0                10.00  10.00  10.00\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I can now notice that metric and stepsize are not changed when algorithm is &quot;HMC&quot;, but it&#39;ll be soon fixed.\r<br>&gt; Otherwise:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; sampler_config &lt;- get_sampler_config(sf, print = FALSE)\r<br>&gt;  &gt; sampler_config\r<br>&gt;    chain_id sampler int_time max_treedepth metric stepsize stepsize_jitter iter\r<br>&gt; 1        1     HMC 9.424778            NA   &lt;NA&gt;       NA              NA   10\r<br>&gt; 2        2    NUTS       NA            12 unit_e      0.7               0  100\r<br>&gt; 3        3    NUTS       NA            15 diag_e      0.5               0  500\r<br>&gt;    warmup thin engaged gamma delta kappa t0\r<br>&gt; 1      5    1    TRUE  0.05  0.61  0.75 10\r<br>&gt; 2     50   10    TRUE  0.05  0.62  0.75 10\r<br>&gt; 3    250   50    TRUE  0.05  0.63  0.75 10\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; A data frame. As to get_sampler_params():\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; get_sampler_params(sf)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Chain 1 (HMC):\r<br>&gt;                Min. 1st Qu. Median   Mean 3rd Qu.  Max.\r<br>&gt; accept_stat 0.0000  0.2173 0.7094 0.5975   1.000 1.000\r<br>&gt; stepsize    0.3383  1.5630 1.5630 1.7300   1.671 4.800\r<br>&gt; int_time    9.4250  9.4250 9.4250 9.4250   9.425 9.425\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Chain 2 (NUTS):\r<br>&gt;                   Min. 1st Qu. Median   Mean 3rd Qu. Max.\r<br>&gt; accept_stat 2.232e-32  0.2365 0.4477 0.5134   0.927  1.0\r<br>&gt; stepsize    4.814e-01  1.5500 1.5500 1.6700   1.572  2.8\r<br>&gt; treedepth   0.000e+00  0.0000 0.0000 0.2000   0.000  1.0\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Chain 3 (NUTS):\r<br>&gt;                Min. 1st Qu. Median   Mean 3rd Qu.  Max.\r<br>&gt; accept_stat  0.000 0.02386 0.2003 0.3332  0.5172  1.00\r<br>&gt; stepsize     1.896 2.02900 2.1150 3.7140  2.1150 11.78\r<br>&gt; treedepth   -1.000 0.00000 0.0000 0.0000  0.0000  1.00\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Or:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; sampler_params &lt;- get_sampler_params(sf, print = FALSE)\r<br>&gt;  &gt; sampler_params\r<br>&gt;     chain algorithm   accept_stat int_time treedepth\r<br>&gt; 1      1       HMC  0.000000e+00 9.424778        NA\r<br>&gt; 2      1       HMC  1.805636e-42 9.424778        NA\r<br>&gt; ...\r<br>&gt; 29     3      NUTS  5.472281e-01       NA         0\r<br>&gt; 30     3      NUTS  2.905030e-02       NA         0\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Another data frame. Furthermore,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; print(sf)\r<br>&gt; Inference for Stan model: normal.\r<br>&gt; 3 chains, each with iter=10; warmup=5; thin=1;\r<br>&gt; ...\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; is wrong, because n_save and warmup2 are equal, but iter/warmup/thin are not.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; If someone thinks that such pedantic &quot;improvements&quot; could be useful, I&#39;ll polish up and submit my code.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Sergio\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; --\r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;stan users mailing list&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467613266000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_qvhSR0QA3Bc7R6vlMNYW\">https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out</a>.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
